(*"group_schema.group"
A **group** is an identification of a collection of elements.
*)


(*"group_schema.group.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **group** is known.
*)


(*"group_schema.group.name.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.group.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **group**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"group_schema.group.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **group**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"group_schema.group.id.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to group as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"group_schema.group.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.group.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.group.wr:WR1"
Each **group** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item,identified_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>.
*)


(*"group_schema.group.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"group_schema.group.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"group_schema.group_relationship"
A **group_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:group_schema.group,group>> with a description of their relationship.
*)


(*"group_schema.group_relationship.__note"
The role of *group_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.group_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"group_schema.group_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:group_schema.group,group>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"group_schema.group_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **group_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"group_schema.group_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **group_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"group_schema.group_relationship.relating_group"
one of the instances of <<express:group_schema.group,group>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"group_schema.group_relationship.relating_group.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.group_relationship.related_group"
the other instance of <<express:group_schema.group,group>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"group_schema.group_relationship.related_group.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship"
The **acyclic_group_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:group_schema.group,group>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:group_schema.group_relationship,group_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:group_schema.group_relationship,group_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:group_schema.group_relationship,group_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:group_schema.group,group>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:group_schema.group_relationship.relating_group,relating_group>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"group_schema.acyclic_group_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:group_schema.group_relationship,group_relationship>> entity.
*)


